WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:08.450
Hey, David, will Republicans support an election
day, an election delay, rather, if Donald

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.850
Trump is definitely going to lose?

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:18.300
So this is an interesting question because
it first assumes that Republicans or Trump

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.720
ists might come to the conclusion that Trump
definitely is going to lose.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.800
I don't think the average Trump ist is going
to believe that going into November.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.820
In other words, the average Trump ist no matter
what.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.440
If Trump says he's doing well in the polls,
which he's been saying, even though he's not.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.530
They will believe Trump has a chance.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:43.100
So in practice, I don't think this scenario
is going to come up because you're not going

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:48.989
to convince the vast majority of Trump ists
that Trump is is going to lose.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:51.159
Let's imagine you did.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:54.510
Would they then support an election delay
if Trump wanted it?

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.510
Absolutely.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.170
If there's one thing we've learned during
this presidency, it's that anything Trump

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.459
wants, his followers want.

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:09.640
If it's the authoritarian deployment of paramilitaries
with no badges and unmarked vans to Portland

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.580
and Chicago and wherever, even if they thought
they were small government, conservative libertarians

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.730
or whatever, up until that they're supporting
it, no question about it.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:22.930
When it's trump against vote by mail, they're
against vote by mail.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.780
Trump comes out, as he did last week or the
week before and says in Florida, it's safe

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.920
and everybody should vote by mail.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.170
They immediately fall in line and they say,
yes, yes, everybody should be voting by mail

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.670
because Donald Trump said so.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:40.430
So if Donald Trump were to Trump has floated
it.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.071
He's not said we need to delay, but he's floated
it.

00:01:43.071 --> 00:01:45.800
And he said we might not know the results
for weeks or years.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.730
He even said, which is absolutely ridiculous.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.870
If Trump actually came out and said, I believe
we should delay the election to whatever date,

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.870
it would be crazy, right.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.330
There'd be no legal basis for it.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:02.600
Of course, a huge portion of his followers
will fall in line because they fall in line

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.010
with absolutely anything that he says.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:09.539
We have to make sure that we start voting
now.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:15.709
I mean, there are states wherein I think,
is it two and a half weeks or three weeks?

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:18.889
Early voting, absentee ballots start.

00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:22.489
We have to overwhelm the vote so that it's
not close.

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:26.840
And we need to just remember that a federal
election has never been delayed.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.510
There have never been delays to presidential
elections.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.290
His followers are liable to support absolutely
anything that he wants.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:38.720
Well, we have to make sure we do is to vote,
participate.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.940
Keep the pressure on as far as the post office.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.349
Keep the pressure on as far as vote by mail.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:47.579
And none of this stuff is really going to
become an issue.

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:53.469
And I'm not sure I understand why I'm getting
so many questions like will Republicans support

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:54.690
delaying the election?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.480
Or will the military be required to remove
Donald Trump?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.480
I get it.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.120
I understand why that's going on.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.499
And it's because many of you are willing to
crawl over broken glass to vote in November

00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:09.140
one way or the other by mail or in person,
because you see the importance of removing

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.140
Donald Trump.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.329
I get it.

00:03:11.329 --> 00:03:14.340
I do not believe it's actually going to come
to that.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.250
I do not believe we are going to have any
serious possibility of an election delay.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.810
I do not believe that if Donald Trump loses,
the military will be required to remove him.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.519
I do not believe it.

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:26.859
These could be famous last words.

00:03:26.859 --> 00:03:33.620
I will eat my hat if it ends up working out
that way in November into January.

